diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index e3cc20704d79de72cb7c2dad23596de78afd0e5b..1b119d22cf9b86bac474a9832164c5b6e02081bb 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -13,3 +13,11 @@ Prices are integer cents everywhere. Run the tests with `npm test`.
 `SPRING10` takes 10 % off the items (a half cent rounds up); `WELCOME5` takes 5.00 € off, on items of 30.00 € or
 more. An unknown code, or `WELCOME5` on a smaller order, is refused and the order is unchanged. Shipping is never
 discounted and free shipping is decided on the items before the discount. `totals` reports `discountCents`.
+
+## Monthly export
+
+`orders.exportMonth('YYYY-MM')` returns CSV text for the accountant's spreadsheet: a header line
+(`order,date,customer,total`), then one line per order placed in that month, by order number. Customers' email addresses and phone numbers are deliberately left out. `date` is
+as the order stores it; `total` is what the customer pays (items less discount, plus shipping) in euros with two
+decimals. A value with a comma, quote or line break is quoted, quotes doubled. A month without orders gives the header
+line alone; a month not written `YYYY-MM` is refused. Every line, the header included, ends with a newline.
